        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43658</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43658"/>
        <updated>2026-04-08T19:17:36.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43302.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4007765391" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43302" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43302/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43302">#43302</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">We didn't have a standalone page for <code class="notranslate">integrity</code>, and since it's a bit involved and used in more than one element. I thought it was worth creating one.</p>
<p dir="auto">I've talked about including multiple hash values, and the behavior as I understand it.</p>
<p dir="auto">TBH I don't understand why anyone would provide more than one hash function rather than just use SHA-512. Maybe I'm missing something?</p>
<p dir="auto">I haven't systematically rewritten the SRI guide, just made some changes that seemed necessary.</p>
<p dir="auto">I would be tempted to remove a lot of the detail about "how to generate hashes" and just point people at tools like OpenSSL.</p>]]></content>
